Fetch_And_Add(X,i)

   is an atomic Read-Modify-Write instruction that reads the value of memory location $X$, increments it by the value $i$, and returns the old value of $X$. It is used in the pseudocode shown below to implement a busy-wait lock. $L$ is an unsigned integer shared variable initialized to $0$. The value of $0$ corresponds to lock being available, while any non-zero value corresponds to the lock being not available.


AcquireLock(L){
   while (Fetch_And_Add(L,1)) 
      L = 1;
}

ReleaseLock(L){ 
